{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera","id":1509634,"title":"Do Rites work for all Fera?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T15:54:33-07:00","id":1509634,"title":"Do Rites work for all Fera?","content":"Way back when I first got introduced to WTA, I was under the impression that most Rites that the Garou had were a sort of common use variety, while the Rites that other Fera had were strictly their own, and only presented because we were seeing the what magic was uniquely their own.<br /> <br /> Rite of the Spirit Egg is obviously only a Corax Rite, but I also understood that one Gurhal Rite that frees Fomori was also a strictly werebear Rite that could not be cast by anyone else. I am asking about this because the Grondr Rite where you can eat Banes is explicitly something a Garou CAN use, but probably shouldn\u2019t unless he has some seriously powerful merits that allows him to resist Wyrm corruption and possession. What about the Apis lvl 4 Rite that allows you to incubate new shapeshifters in the ground? Can a Corax or Bastet learn this Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:07:10-07:00","id":1509638,"title":"","content":"I think the lost rites like that need special dispensation to be learned or performed. They will never be learned en masse and the spirits that make them work will be rare and hard to appease. So while anyone might be able to learn them by doing the right things with the right spirits and finding the lost knowledge, having them is a whole story of its own.<br /> <br /> Past Lives is a whole chronicle about the history of the Fera that finishes with certain gifts and rites coming back with the PC's. It's a campaign's worth of story to get there, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:49:49-07:00","id":1509644,"title":"","content":"Could the spirit that makes it work possibly be Earth? As in the Gaian counterpart to H\u2019rugg, the Essence of Sludge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:02:51-07:00","id":1509645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1509644#post1509644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the spirit that makes it work possibly be Earth? As in the Gaian counterpart to H\u2019rugg, the Essence of Sludge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. Something like that would be more an elemental than what you're after. Past Lives says it's the Ancestors Spirits of the dead breeds that allow you to use their gifts/rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:15:42-07:00","id":1509648,"title":"","content":"K, but then who originally powered the Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T18:49:35-07:00","id":1509673,"title":"","content":"Rites work because the spirits in general respond to them when correctly performed by spiritual beings, i.e. Garou, Fera, and some Possessed. Exactly which spirits depends; mostly, for Garou and Fera rites, it's naturae, but Ananasi have more truck with Triatic manifestations, and the rites that the Dying Cubs camp of the Red Talons discovered came from some other, nebulous source, about which the only certain thing was that it wasn't Gaia. Then, you have the Rite of Sacred Rebirth, which usually invokes the spirits of the Wyrm unless you're using the free sacrifice clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:21:09-07:00","id":1509742,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Saur Ops is right. There are some exotic teachers, but most of them are Naturae as the spirits closest to the Garou. The idea is that Rites and Gifts work thanks to the pacts and agreements with the Spirits. For the extinct breeds these pacts and agreements cannot be upheld by the lost breeds. One would need to rebuild these relationships and one might think the spirits might be holding grudges over their losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T08:18:20-07:00","id":1509868,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to wonder whether Rites would work in a space prepared by Mages (with Spirit-based warding) or Changelings (using Guest List from Sovereign) to block the input of spirits.<br /> <br /> If a Rite of Purification is attempted in a space where Naturae and other relevant spirits simply can't reach, does it fail by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:23:49-07:00","id":1509877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1509868#post1509868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to wonder whether Rites would work in a space prepared by Mages (with Spirit-based warding) or Changelings (using Guest List from Sovereign) to block the input of spirits.<br /> <br /> If a Rite of Purification is attempted in a space where Naturae and other relevant spirits simply can't reach, does it fail by default?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is exactly the reason given for why rites typically fail in Malfeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T23:37:06-07:00","id":1509928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1509877#post1509877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter is exactly the reason given for why rites typically fail in Malfeas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reasoning should apply to the Shadowlands, right? I can't recall whether it is explicitly stated somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T06:58:11-07:00","id":1509953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1509928#post1509928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same reasoning should apply to the Shadowlands, right? I can't recall whether it is explicitly stated somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly possibly but nowhere near as absolute as in Malfeas. The shadowlands are a picnic in comparison to the snarl that marks where the universe has been twisted and torn off its proper axis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T23:03:21-07:00","id":1510679,"title":"","content":"Speaking of this, Gurahl has a Rite called Fighting the Death Bear which allows you to defeat the Incarna Bear's aspcet of Death and make one guy back to life, I also think that's a Gurahl-limited rite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T00:47:43-07:00","id":1510688,"title":"","content":"I think all the shifters have their own rites, and there is just an overlap among the most useful ones. You can imagine that even if a cat shifter can't learn the garou's rite of dedication, they probably created their own version of it. There is definitely some werewolf ones that doesn't make sense for other shifters to have. It is kind of up to the person running the game to determine which rituals each shifter race might know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T06:26:30-07:00","id":1510977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1509742#post1509742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Saur Ops is right. There are some exotic teachers, but most of them are Naturae as the spirits closest to the Garou. <b>The idea is that Rites and Gifts work thanks to the pacts and agreements with the Spirits.</b> For the extinct breeds these pacts and agreements cannot be upheld by the lost breeds. One would need to rebuild these relationships and one might think the spirits might be holding grudges over their losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong here but I seem to recall that gifts and rites are very different - gifts don't invoke the power of the spirit, just the being that invokes them. It's why spirits can't take them back once they are given. While Rites work as you state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T07:49:47-07:00","id":1510980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1510977#post1510977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be wrong here but I seem to recall that gifts and rites are very different - gifts don't invoke the power of the spirit, just the being that invokes them. It's why spirits can't take them back once they are given. While Rites work as you state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Gifts are learned within the bounds of a larger pact that a group of changers has with a broad category of spirits. If a spirit isn't within that pact, learning anything from them gets a lot more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T08:00:56-07:00","id":1510982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1510679#post1510679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of this, Gurahl has a Rite called Fighting the Death Bear which allows you to defeat the Incarna Bear's aspcet of Death and make one guy back to life, I also think that's a Gurahl-limited rite</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons the War of Rage broke out, becasue the Garou wanted this secret, but the Gurahl belived they are not ready nor should have it - it is not really they couldn't had it, but the Bear wouldn't teach them<br /> And there is the other end of the spectrum so to speak, the Mokol\u00e9 (and to an extent the Croax) with the Mnesis, but there is a catch! Mokol\u00e9 can only remember things an ancestor might have seen or done or known... but the Kinfolk is a nice bridge to this; there is no such thing a homid Garou kinflok, a homid Mokol\u00e9 kinflok, a homid bastes kinflok, etc. you get the drift, there is only Human Kinfolk. Your human kin's great great great great great grandfather could have been a Garou. And when you enter the Mnesis, in your own little ubble of memopry, where all of your ancestors wait in an amphitheatre like scene; in the first row your two parents, second row, four grand parents, third row, eight great grand parent and so on upt to the distant Lizard Kings silhouettes at the &quot;top&quot; row? You can easly spot a a few very confused Garou ancestor, apis, or anything basically in your familly - depending of your mnesis trait, how far back you can see.<br /> The racial memory is limited up to the history of a small territory, since clutches are mostly sedentary... but this is the reason why the so-called Wanderers are so valuable between the lizard people: they are Mokol\u00e9 who travel and have contact with different clutches everywhere, sharing memories between their kind and even mating with the local kinflok, avoiding inbreeding and renewing the knowledge of the clutch. And on top of that, they could use the Fetish, Bowl of Mnesis<br /> The point is, as the Beats Court and the Ahadi demonstrated, when the Fera work together, they could ,should and would share gifts and rites as Gaia intended them to work together for Her<br /> (More or less, I always preferred the Rokea aproach of the world in that regard; Unsea aka. the dry land (gaia) just panicked an created all bunch of shifters, because realized if Sea and Kun made the Rokea to <i>Survive</i> even if Qyrl manages to close the Great Wound (the sun) she made on Oversea (sky) and everything will be dark and cold again... then what will happen with her and the life on her? She made the Garou to be her Claws and Fangs to fight against a great enemy, not unlike Nightmare, but there was none... so without a real porpouse, they started to fight and kill everything. Make sense in a poetic way)<br /> <br /> So it is not really the question those rites and gifts would work, more like who would trust a Garou enough to teach them after two War of Rages and several genocides and their behaviour?<br /> Of course there is always an option...<br /> Good old Minotaur<br /> Minotaur is a shady (at best) Totem (corruption actually) but not tainted and he is not directly allied with the Wyrm (In the events of Skinner, Minotaur begins to drift into the Black Spiral Labyrinth thanks to the machinations of Tick, who seeks to supplant Minotaur as the Totem of the Skin Dancers. The players can decide his fate and possibly even cleanse him. - now Tick is an ancient jaggling, allied to Gaia, but not well respected among her Courts, he is a Totem of Cunning. With ambitions...)<br /> Minotaur is the embodiment of the man that becomes the beast, the sentient being who craves animalistic power. He respects only strength and despises weakness in every form. He is misogynistic to some degree... (my headcanon, Minotaur was the original Apis patron, but after the Apis went down, he became from the Wise Auroch the survivor and strong Minotaur)<br /> Through his parlance his follwoers learn any Gift, any from any other spirits. His ban is that a follower of him has to act out his rivalry against Pegasus and her chosen tribe, the Black Furies.<br /> And if you think about is, that is HUGE and a good evidance, you only need a teacher...<br /> He is not that bad, Wendigo is a cannibal spirit of winter, grim and dark, Grandfather Thunder teaches you gifts to hide your Taint, Uktena? Oh boy, lets not start on that one! Griffin is insane and bloodthirsty. And Fenrir may or may not want to devour Helios like in the viking propheices and Cockroach forbid the Glass Walkers to act against the Samsa, the Mockery Breed of cockroach-shifters...<br /> To be honest, Minotaur is not even in the top three &quot;bad boy&quot; spirits even with his interest of the Skin Dancers to have as a personal or pack totem, nor have the worse of bans (heck, some Tribes even would be more than happy to act against Pegasus and the Furies...)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T09:03:25-07:00","id":1510986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1510977#post1510977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be wrong here but I seem to recall that gifts and rites are very different - gifts don't invoke the power of the spirit, just the being that invokes them. It's why spirits can't take them back once they are given. While Rites work as you state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts are intrinsic parts of who you are. Rites are invocations and proper procedural elements and sacrifices to the spirits to allow them to intercede in the world or affect the world. Rites are by their nature extrinsic. They both come from the Spirits and the relationship the Garou have with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:51:12-07:00","id":1511006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509634-do-rites-work-for-all-fera?p=1510986#post1510986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gifts are intrinsic parts of who you are. Rites are invocations and proper procedural elements and sacrifices to the spirits to allow them to intercede in the world or affect the world. Rites are by their nature extrinsic. They both come from the Spirits and the relationship the Garou have with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I meant that, Spirits don't actually power the gifts, the Garou does. Spirits, however power the rites. Remove the spirits, the gifts still works as long as the Garou already knows them, but remove the spirits and the Rites don't. So, knowledge of both gifts and rites cames from the spirits once, yes, but the effect of the gifts themselves don't, only the Rites. So, for example, a Black Spiral conducting a gaian rite might have no results because the spirits might refuse to acknowledge her, but the same black spiral that learned a gaian sourced gift when they were a child of gaia (we're assuming a pretty dramatic fall here) will still get to use that gift with impunity, and the spirits can do nothing about it because the power comes from her now. (They can hunt her down and kill her, of course, but that's a different story).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}